+<section class="tp-hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="product-title"><div class="tp-hero-copy"><p class="tp-eyebrow"><a href="/products/scenepilot/">ScenePilot</a><span>Public web alpha</span></p><h1 id="product-title">AutoCut</h1><p class="tp-promise">Give your footage a rhythm.</p><p class="tp-intro">Bring your clips and a soundtrack. Build a beat-aware first cut, keep the moments you love, then refine the result in ScenePilot.</p><div class="tp-actions"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://scenepilot.thecreatingco.com/tools/autocut/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open AutoCut <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a><a class="tp-secondary" href="#make">Choose a first project</a></div></div><figure class="tp-workspace"><button type="button" data-tp-preview aria-label="Enlarge AutoCut preview" title="Enlarge preview"><img src="/assets/tool-products/autocut.webp" width="1440" height="960" alt="Actual AutoCut workspace with existing demo media; not evidence of broad real-footage qualification." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></button><figcaption>Actual AutoCut workspace with existing demo media; not evidence of broad real-footage qualification.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="tcc-product-story" data-product-story="autocut" style="--story-accent:#b8a3ff" aria-labelledby="product-story-autocut-title"><div class="tcc-story-heading"><p class="tcc-story-kicker">A VISUAL TOUR · AUTOCUT</p><h2 id="product-story-autocut-title">The work, as it comes together.</h2><p>Start with footage and a song, then explore beat-aware cut controls. AutoCut is an alpha; results depend on material and device.</p></div><div class="tcc-story-layout"><div class="tcc-story-visual" data-story-visual><div class="tcc-story-frames"><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-autocut-1" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/creative-tools/autocut.webp" alt="AutoCut starting screen showing where to add a song and clips." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>AutoCut starting screen showing where to add a song and clips.</figcaption></figure><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-autocut-2" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/tool-products/autocut.webp" alt="AutoCut actual workspace with a sample project loaded." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>AutoCut actual workspace with a sample project loaded.</figcaption></figure></div><nav class="tcc-story-controls" data-story-controls role="tablist" aria-label="AutoCut visual tour" hidden></nav></div><div class="tcc-story-copy"><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Start with your footage</h3><p>Choose clips and music to begin a beat-aware edit.</p></article><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">02 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Shape a cut</h3><p>Explore style, pace and framing controls in a sample workspace.</p></article><p class="tcc-story-status tcc-story-sr-only" data-story-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Start with the soundtrack</h3><p>Let the track&#x27;s beat and energy guide a first sequence.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Keep your decisions</h3><p>Compare cut presets, re-roll and lock the shots you want to keep.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Keep editing</h3><p>Move the cut into ScenePilot instead of treating the first result as final.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A release-day teaser</option><option value="1">A product in motion</option><option value="2">Performance takes</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A release-day teaser</h3><p>Turn a handful of performance clips into a short announcement.</p><ol><li>Choose a short soundtrack section with a clear beat and import your clips.</li><li>Compare a calmer preset with a faster cut; lock one strong opening shot.</li><li>Review the sequence, then refine titles and transitions in ScenePilot.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A product in motion</h3><p>Give a collection of detail shots a shared pace.</p><ol><li>Import wide, close-up and detail shots alongside a soundtrack.</li><li>Generate a first cut and keep shots that clearly show the product.</li><li>Check the framing for your intended aspect ratio before export.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">Performance takes</h3><p>Explore a first edit using multiple takes of the same performance.</p><ol><li>Use takes with clean reference audio and the same song.</li><li>Review the suggested alignment and every cut between takes.</li><li>Correct anything that drifts in the editor; do not assume alignment is exact.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://scenepilot.thecreatingco.com/tools/autocut/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in AutoCut <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Review the cut and export before leaving. Keep your original media; a browser session is not a backup.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>Rendered video</dt><dd>Encoding and format availability depend on the browser.</dd></div><div><dt>ScenePilot handoff</dt><dd>Continue refining the generated edit.</dd></div><div><dt>Shot list</dt><dd>Keep a readable record of the selected shots.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=autocut#feedback">Send AutoCut feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>AutoCut makes a first cut, not a finished film. Beat detection and multi-take alignment can be wrong. Prior end-to-end evidence uses generated footage; broad real-footage and Safari export testing remain outstanding.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Review the cut and export before leaving. Keep your original media; a browser session is not a backup.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
