l" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/creative-tools/board.webp" alt="Board starting workspace for a film-planning project." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Board starting workspace for a film-planning project.</figcaption></figure><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-board-2" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/tool-products/board.webp" alt="Board actual workspace with a planning example." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Board actual workspace with a planning example.</figcaption></figure></div><nav class="tcc-story-controls" data-story-controls role="tablist" aria-label="Board visual tour" hidden></nav></div><div class="tcc-story-copy"><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Begin with the idea</h3><p>Bring a script or outline into a film-planning workspace.</p></article><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">02 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Make the plan visible</h3><p>Explore the Board workspace for shot-list and storyboard planning.</p></article><p class="tcc-story-status tcc-story-sr-only" data-story-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>A useful first pass</h3><p>Generate scenes and suggested shots from screenplay-style text or prose.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Make each shot yours</h3><p>Edit the lens, duration and shot type; sketch or upload a reference.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Take the plan with you</h3><p>Print to PDF, export CSV or save a board JSON file.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A three-shot product film</option><option value="1">A performance video</option><option value="2">A tiny narrative</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A three-shot product film</h3><p>Plan an opening, a detail and a reveal.</p><ol><li>Write three beats: establish the object, show a detail, reveal the whole.</li><li>Generate the board and replace guessed framing with your own choices.</li><li>Sketch a reference for each shot and export the plan.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A performance video</h3><p>Plan coverage before recording multiple takes.</p><ol><li>Outline the song sections and where you want different setups.</li><li>Add a wide, medium and close-up; review lens and duration suggestions.</li><li>Print the board and use it as a shoot checklist.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">A tiny narrative</h3><p>Make a short scene legible before finding a camera.</p><ol><li>Paste a short scene with a location and a clear action.</li><li>Reorder or duplicate shots to establish the sequence you want.</li><li>Save the board JSON before trying a ScenePilot handoff.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://scenepilot.thecreatingco.com/tools/board/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Board <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Browser autosave is local to that browser. Export board JSON for a portable copy; print or export CSV for the shoot.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>Print to PDF</dt><dd>A shoot-ready document through the browser print dialog.</dd></div><div><dt>CSV / board JSON</dt><dd>A shot list or a portable board file.</dd></div><div><dt>ScenePilot markers</dt><dd>Scene/shot markers and the written brief; sketches stay in Board.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=board#feedback">Send Board feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>Parsing and shot suggestions are heuristics, not creative decisions. Review guessed lenses and durations. The ScenePilot import can replace the open project: save that project first. Sketches do not travel with the marker handoff.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Browser autosave is local to that browser. Export board JSON for a portable copy; print or export CSV for the shoot.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
