itle": "Forest landscape", "description": "Explore the prepared Forest landscape project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Terrain / displacement / landscape / STL", "level": "Explore", "firstMove": "Explore a surface variation and its export.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=terrain", "poster": "/assets/form-studies/terrain-perspective.jpg", "key": "form:terrain"}, {"product": "luma", "id": "cinema", "title": "Build a cinematic scene.", "description": "Combine the character and hooded scene from the two supplied boards. Paint in the atmosphere and compare moonlight with an amber grade.", "skills": "Mask painting / compositing / Curves / mood studies", "level": "Explore", "time": "7\u201310 min", "firstMove": "Use the first step in the real Luma lesson to change the prepared project.", "url": "/learn/luma/workshops/?workshop=cinema", "poster": "/assets/luma-workshops/cinema-example.jpg", "key": "luma:cinema"}, {"product": "form", "id": "dimensions", "title": "Make it your size", "description": "Explore the prepared Make it your size project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Dimensions / CAD / precision / geometry", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Enter a new dimension in the prepared design.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=dimensions", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:dimensions"}, {"product": "luma", "id": "compose", "title": "Eight layers. Your composition.", "description": "Reorder the stack, move the imagery and edit the headline. Continue with this exact document in the next lesson.", "skills": "8 editable layers / layer order / placement / live text", "level": "First steps", "time": "5\u20137 min", "firstMove": "Select a layer, move it, then change the order of the eight-layer composition.", "url": "/learn/luma/workshops/?workshop=compose", "poster": "/assets/luma-workshops/compose-example.jpg", "key": "luma:compose"}, {"product": "form", "id": "history", "title": "See how it was made", "description": "Explore the prepared See how it was made project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "History / sketch / extrude / bevel", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Inspect how the object\u2019s features build its shape.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=history", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:history"}, {"product": "luma", "id": "effects", "title": "Same layers. A different feeling.", "description": "Continue your composition and explore all 27 blend modes, 17 layer effects and 15 editable smart filters.", "skills": "Blending / opacity / layer effects / smart filters / blend modes", "level": "Explore", "time": "6\u20139 min", "firstMove": "Keep your eight-layer composition and try a blend mode or layer effect.", "url": "/learn/luma/workshops/?workshop=effects", "poster": "/assets/luma-workshops/effects-example.jpg", "key": "luma:effects"}, {"product": "form", "id": "challenge", "title": "Three objects, one workflow", "description": "Explore the prepared Three objects, one workflow project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Clasp / ring / enclosure / CAD", "level": "Explore", "firstMove": "Try the measured workflow on another object.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=challenge", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:challenge"}, {"product": "form", "id": "materials", "title": "Find the right finish", "description": "Explore the prepared Find the right finish project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Materials / finish / roughness / lighting", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Change the finish while keeping the shape.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=materials", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:materials"}, {"product": "form", "id": "handoff", "title": "Keep the editable object", "description": "Explore the prepared Keep the editable object project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Save / project / export / PNG / STL", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Keep an editable project and test an export.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=handoff", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:handoff"}]}</script><details class="secondary-reference"><summary>Explore the workflow &amp; tools<span>Open guide ↗</span></summary><div class="form-origin"><section class="form-section" id="form-origin-workflow" aria-labelledby="form-origin-workflow-heading"><div class="form-section-heading"><p class="form-eyebrow">01 / THE WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="form-origin-workflow-heading">Follow the idea.<br/><span>Not the interface.</span></h2><p class="form-section-intro">Move between free exploration and measured decisions. Keep the process direct—and the result editable.</p></div><div class="form-steps"><article><span class="form-step-number">0<!-- -->1</span><h3>Start with a line.</h3><p>Draw a profile, import an SVG or begin with a reusable primitive. Start simple. The interesting part comes next.</p><small>Sketch tools / SVG import / Primitives</small></article><article><span class="form-step-number">0<!-- -->2</span><h3>Give it dimension.</h3><p>Turn a closed profile into a solid. Pull a face, enter a distance or refine a dimension—in millimeters, inches or degrees.</p><small>Extrude / Direct editing / Exact dimensions</small></article><article><span class="form-step-number">0<!-- -->3</span><h3>Make it your own.</h3><p>Explore modifiers, adjust a finish and compose your scene. Save the editable project so the next idea doesn’t mean starting over.</p><small>Modifiers / Materials / Editable projects</small></article></div></section><section class="form-features" id="form-origin-features" aria-labelledby="form-origin-features-heading"><div class="form-feature-title"><p class="form-eyebrow">02 / BUILT TO KEEP YOU MAKING</p><h2 id="form-origin-features-heading">Fluid ideas.<br/>Exact decisions.</h2><p>Make a buckle. Explore a sculptural object. Refine a part. Choose the tools that suit the work.</p><a href="https://form.thecreatingco.com/studio" class="form-text-link">Find your starting point <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="form-feature-list"><article><span class="form-feature-number">01</span><div><p class="form-eyebrow">Precision CAD</p><h3>Precision, when you need it.</h3><p>Work with dimensions, constraints and feature history. Exact geometry helps you move beyond a good-looking viewport.</p></div></article><article><span class="form-feature-number">02</span><div><p class="form-eyebrow">Creative modeling</p><h3>Room to experiment.</h3><p>Shape creative meshes, apply modifiers and explore material graphs. Undo and Redo keep iteration part of the process.</p></div></article><article><span class="form-feature-number">03</span><div><p class="form-eyebrow">Design generators</p><h3>A useful head start.</h3><p>Begin with purpose-built recipes for hardware, rings and linked systems. Adjust the parameters instead of rebuilding every repeated detail.</p></div></article></div></section><section class="form-fabric form-section" id="form-origin-garment" aria-labelledby="form-origin-fabric-heading"><div><p class="form-eyebrow">03 / BEYOND THE SOLID</p><h2 id="form-origin-fabric-heading">Think in pieces.<br/><span>Explore in fabric.</span></h2><p class="form-section-intro">Draft or trace pattern pieces, connect seams and explore how they drape around adjustable or imported bodies.</p><a href="https://form.thecreatingco.com/studio" class="form-text-link">Open Form, then choose Fabric <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="form-fabric-notes"><span class="form-label">FABRIC WORKSPACE · EXPERIMENTAL</span><dl><div><dt>Pattern</dt><dd>Draw pieces, adjust measurements and set seam allowances.</dd></div><div><dt>Sew</dt><dd>Connect compatible edges and build up a garment.</dd></div><div><dt>Explore</dt><dd>Simulate drape and inspect estimated fit on a body.</dd></div></dl><p class="form-fineprint">Simulation and fit estimates are not physically validated sizing or production approval. Test patterns and materials before manufacturing.</p></div></section></div></details><!-- PRODUCT-REFRESH:START --><!-- PRODUCT-REFRESH:END --><div class="section" style="padding-block:0"></div><!-- FORM-ARCHITECTURE:START --><!-- PRODUCT-LESSONS:START --><!-- PRODUCT-LESSONS:END --><!-- FORM-ARCHITECTURE:END --><!-- FORM-FASHION:START --><!-- FORM-FASHION:END --><!-- FORM-JEWELRY:START --><!-- FORM-JEWELRY:END --><!-- FORM-STUDIES:START --><!-- FORM-STUDIES:END --><!-- SUITE-LEARNING:START --><!-- SUITE-LEARNING:END --><!-- PRODUCT-FEATURES:START --><section class="pf" id="product-features" aria-labelledby="pf-title" data-product-features="form" style="--pf-accent:#d8ff3e"><div class="pf-intro"><div><p class="pf-eyebrow">INSIDE FORM STUDIO</p><h2 id="pf-title">What Form Studio can do.</h2><p class="pf-lede">Design precise products, jewelry, and garments in one editable workspace.</p></div><p class="pf-total"><strong>16</strong><span>features to explore</span></p></div><aside class="pf-scope" aria-label="Edition and availability"><p><strong>Full product inventory. Web, native and experimental capabilities vary by edition.</strong> The browser provides an editable design environment; native geometry, simulation, rendering, and filesystem services differ. Engineering, architectural, and garment outputs require independent review.</p></aside><div class="pr-search"><label for="pr-feature-search">Find a capability</label><input id="pr-feature-search" type="search" data-pr-search placeholder="Search tools, workflows or editions" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="pr-feature-status"><p id="pr-feature-status" data-pr-search-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><nav class="pf-jump" aria-label="Feature categories"><a href="#pf-form-1">Precision &amp; design systems</a><a href="#pf-form-2">Mesh &amp; sculpting</a><a href="#pf-form-3">Fabric, light &amp; motion</a><a href="#pf-form-4">Save, share &amp; exchange</a></nav><details class="pf-group" id="pf-form-1"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Precision &amp; design systems</h3><span class="pf-group-count">6 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Parametric sketching</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Create dimensioned 2D sketches with units, constraints, and editable relationships.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=architecture#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Precision CAD</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Build and rebuild solid geometry using exact geometry operations, including native desktop geometry services.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=architecture#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Editable feature history</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Revisit earlier modeling decisions, adjust parameters, and explore configurations.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Components and assemblies</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Organize reusable parts, assemble components, and define mating relationships.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Technical documentation</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Prepare drawings, quantities, geometric dimensioning and tolerancing metadata, and manufacturing checks.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Design generators</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Start product, engineering, architectural, jewelry, hardware, ring, chain, and linked-system designs from natural-language descriptions or procedural starters.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=architecture#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-form-2"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Mesh &amp; sculpting</h3><span class="pf-group-count">3 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Creative mesh modeling</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Extrude, inset, bevel, insert edge loops, crease edges, transform vertices, and sculpt.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=materials#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Modifier stacks</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Reorder or toggle subdivision, mirroring, arrays, solidification, welding, smoothing, simplification, retopology, bending, twisting, tapering, bulging, and displacement.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Editable sculpting</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Preserve recorded brush strokes and multiresolution sculpt layers instead of immediately flattening every change into geometry.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-form-3"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Fabric, light &amp; motion</h3><span class="pf-group-count">4 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Fabric design</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Draft and grade patterns, define seams, import fit bodies, and inspect fit maps.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=drape#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Cloth simulation</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Explore fabric behavior with layered, self, and avatar collision support; desktop adds native simulation.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/form/?lesson=drape#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Appearance Studio</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Apply persistent physically based materials, compare lighting environments, adjust exposure and shadows, and export the current camera view as PNG.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Animation and Rig workspaces</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Explore animation, rigging, and physics-driven studies; these remain experimental and under evaluation.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-form-4"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Save, share &amp; exchange</h3><span class="pf-group-count">3 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Interchange</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Supported workflows include STEP/BREP, STL, editable DXF, mesh formats, and scoped IFC4/USD handling.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Project continuity</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Versioned `.form` and `.formcad` files, migration of older projects, backups, recovery checkpoints, and atomic native saves.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Optional collaboration</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Authenticated web revisions, shared assets, sharing, and branch/review information.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details></section><!-- PRODUCT-FEATURES:END --><!-- AFTER-HOURS:form:START --><details class="secondary-reference"><summary>Project walkthrough: After Hours<span>Open reference ↗</span></summary><section class="ah" id="after-hours-form" data-after-hours="form" style="--ah-accent:#475c3e"><p class="ah-eyebrow">AFTER HOURS / Form Studio / Web editor</p><h2>A small change. A different presence.</h2><p class="ah-deck">An editable clasp study, from its first proportions to a broader frame and two contrasting metal finishes.</p><div class="ah-chapters" role="tablist" aria-label="Orbit, an adjustable clasp chapters"><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-form-tab-0" aria-controls="after-hours-form-panel-0" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0"><span>01</span>Start with proportion</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-form-tab-1" aria-controls="after-hours-form-panel-1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>02</span>Widen the outer rail</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-form-tab-2" aria-controls="after-hours-form-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>03</span>Bring in warmth</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-form-tab-3" aria-controls="after-hours-form-panel-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>04</span>Keep a cooler option</button></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-form-panel-0" aria-labelledby="after-hours-form-tab-0" ><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/form-01-proportions.png" alt="Form Studio: Start with proportion. The buckle starter establishes a 55 × 38 mm outer profile. Its frame, openings and centre bar remain in the editable feature history." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Start with proportion</h3><p>The buckle starter establishes a 55 × 38 mm outer profile. Its frame, openings and centre bar remain in the editable feature history.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-form-panel-1" aria-labelledby="after-hours-form-tab-1" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/form-02-wider-frame.png" alt="Form Studio: Widen the outer rail. Changing the outer width to 64 mm preserves the openings and gives the right rail more weight. The geometry visibly updates in the same isometric view." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Widen the outer rail</h3><p>Changing the outer width to 64 mm preserves the openings and gives the right rail more weight. The geometry visibly updates in the same isometric view.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-form-panel-2" aria-labelledby="after-hours-form-tab-2" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/form-03-brass.png" alt="Form Studio: Bring in warmth. Polished brass changes the surface to a warmer finish, with roughness at 0.17 and metal at 0.94. The camera and geometry stay fixed for comparison." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Bring in warmth</h3><p>Polished brass changes the surface to a warmer finish, with roughness at 0.17 and metal at 0.94. The camera and geometry stay fixed for comparison.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-form-panel-3" aria-labelledby="after-hours-form-tab-3" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/form-04-steel.png" alt="Form Studio: Keep a cooler option. Brushed steel offers a cooler alternative. The finished state was saved as an editable Form project and exported to a verified PNG." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Keep a cooler option</h3><p>Brushed steel offers a cooler alternative. The finished state was saved as an editable Form project and exported to a verified PNG.</p></div></div><p class="ah-count" data-ah-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="ah-actions"><a class="ah-primary" href="https://form.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open Form Studio ↗</a><button type="button" data-ah-expand>Inspect the screenshot</button><button type="button" data-ah-toggle-compare aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="after-hours-form-compare">Compare the finishes</button></div><div class="ah-output" id="after-hours-form-compare" data-ah-comparison hidden><h3>Compare the finishes</h3><div class="ah-compare"><img src="/assets/after-hours/form-03-brass.png" alt="Polished brass" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"><img class="ah-after" src="/assets/after-hours/form-04-steel.png" alt="Brushed steel" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-compare-labels"><span>Polished brass</span><span>Brushed steel</span></div><label for="after-hours-form-range">Comparison divider <output for="after-hours-form-range">50%</output></label><input class="ah-comparison-control" id="after-hours-form-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Comparison divider"></div><div class="ah-actions"><a href="/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-clasp.form" download>Download the editable clasp</a><a href="/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png" download>View the exported PNG</a></div><p class="ah-note">Actual browser session. The starter’s optional fillet failed and was suppressed; these views show the resulting rectangular geometry. This is a visual study, not manufacturing or fit validation.</p><dialog aria-labelledby="after-hours-form-dialog-title"><button type="button" autofocus>Close screenshot</button><p id="after-hours-form-dialog-title" data-ah-dialog-title></p><img alt=""></dialog></section></details><!-- AFTER-HOURS:form:END --><section class="scope-section section" id="browser"><div><p class="overline">YOUR BROWSER EDITION</p><h2>Your web edition.</h2><p>Create editable geometry, explore materials, and save a Form project in the browser.</p><details open><summary>Current limitations</summary><p>Native geometry, simulation, filesystem integration and rendering differ from the web edition. Browser work is not certification for manufacturing, engineering or garment fit.</p></details></div><div class="try-card"><h3>One good first test</h3><ol><li><span>01</span>Open the editor and choose a starter.</li><li><span>02</span>Change dimensions or a material.</li><li><span>03</span>Save a project and test an export.</li></ol><a class="button accent primary-app" href="https://form.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open the browser app</a><a href="/testing/?product=form#feedback">Send feedback</a></div></section><section class="section prose" id="cast"><p class="overline">PREVIEW</p><h2>Cast: jewelry checks for Form Studio.</h2><p>Cast is merged to the Form Studio codebase but not yet on this production site &mdash; try it on its review build. It handles ring sizing, thin-wall and prong checks, mesh health with repair, metal weight estimates, and resin print orientation, with STL export. Estimates only; material minimums still need a caster&rsquo;s sign-off. <a href="https://form-studio-review.netlify.app/studio">Open the Cast preview <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a> (&#9776; project menu &rarr; Open Cast)</p></section><!-- PRODUCT-NEXT:START --><section class="pr-next" aria-labelledby="pr-next-title"><p class="pr-kicker">THE FOUR-PRODUCT CREATIVE SUITE</p><h2 id="pr-next-title">Keep the idea moving.</h2><div class="pr-cards"><a class="pr-card" href="/products/luma/" style="--pr-tone:#ff83ba"><h3>Luma Studio</h3><p>Turn your images into a visual world