 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Guides for a shared rhythm</h3><p>Draw against baseline, x-height, cap-height and descender guides.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>From strokes to type</h3><p>Compile brush or pen strokes into straight-segment outlines.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Use it in your artwork</h3><p>Export OTF/TTF and install the font in Luma&#x27;s Type tool.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">An exhibition wordmark</option><option value="1">A handmade alphabet</option><option value="2">Numbers for a poster</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">An exhibition wordmark</h3><p>Start with the letters needed for one short title.</p><ol><li>Open Glyph font maker from Luma&#x27;s studio menu.</li><li>Draw a few letters with a consistent baseline and cap height.</li><li>Install the font in Luma, then build a title with the Type tool.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A handmade alphabet</h3><p>Explore a shared stroke style across several characters.</p><ol><li>Choose a brush or pen and draw a small set of related letters.</li><li>Preview a word and revise inconsistent widths or proportions.</li><li>Export OTF or TTF to keep a copy outside the browser.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">Numbers for a poster</h3><p>Make a small display set for dates or edition numbers.</p><ol><li>Draw the numerals needed for your design.</li><li>Check how they align against the same guides and metrics.</li><li>Use the installed font on a text layer and save the font separately.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Glyph <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a><p class="tp-entry">In Luma Studio, open the studio menu and choose Glyph font maker.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Export the font as well as your artwork. A browser-installed font is local to that browser and is not an account backup.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>OTF / TTF</dt><dd>Fonts made from straight-segment outlines.</dd></div><div><dt>Install in Luma</dt><dd>Available to the Type tool in this browser.</dd></div><div><dt>Font project</dt><dd>Use Save project to keep an editable copy of your letterforms.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=glyph#feedback">Send Glyph feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>This embedded Glyph has no curve fitting, hinting, kerning, accents or bold/italic styles. Undrawn characters fall back to another font. Installing a font here does not embed it into .luma or PSD files.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Export the font as well as your artwork. A browser-installed font is local to that browser and is not an account backup.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details><details><summary>How is this different from Glyph Studio?</summary><p>Glyph is the simpler font maker inside Luma. <a href="/products/glyph-studio/">Standalone Glyph Studio</a> adds curve fitting and kerning; kerning exports to TTF only.</p></details></div></div></section>
