+<section class="tp-hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="product-title"><div class="tp-hero-copy"><p class="tp-eyebrow"><a href="/products/scenepilot/">ScenePilot</a><span>Public web alpha</span></p><h1 id="product-title">Grade</h1><p class="tp-promise">Find a look. Make it your own.</p><p class="tp-intro">Bring a reference still and your image or clip. Compare a statistical color transfer, adjust its strength and export a graded still or .cube LUT.</p><div class="tp-actions"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://scenepilot.thecreatingco.com/tools/grade/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Grade <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a><a class="tp-secondary" href="#make">Choose a first project</a></div></div><figure class="tp-workspace"><button type="button" data-tp-preview aria-label="Enlarge Grade preview" title="Enlarge preview"><img src="/assets/tool-products/grade.webp" width="1440" height="960" alt="Actual Grade workspace, captured in the public web app. Example project." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></button><figcaption>Actual Grade workspace, captured in the public web app. Example project.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="tcc-product-story" data-product-story="grade" style="--story-accent:#b8a3ff" aria-labelledby="product-story-grade-title"><div class="tcc-story-heading"><p class="tcc-story-kicker">A VISUAL TOUR · GRADE</p><h2 id="product-story-grade-title">The work, as it comes together.</h2><p>Find a look in a reference, then explore a transfer to your clip. Grade is an alpha; results depend on source material.</p></div><div class="tcc-story-layout"><div class="tcc-story-visual" data-story-visual><div class="tcc-story-frames"><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-grade-1" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/creative-tools/grade.webp" alt="Grade starting workspace with reference and clip drop zones." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Grade starting workspace with reference and clip drop zones.</figcaption></figure><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-grade-2" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/tool-products/grade.webp" alt="Grade actual workspace capture showing transfer and export controls." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Grade actual workspace capture showing transfer and export controls.</figcaption></figure></div><nav class="tcc-story-controls" data-story-controls role="tablist" aria-label="Grade visual tour" hidden></nav></div><div class="tcc-story-copy"><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Choose a reference</h3><p>Start with a still whose color and contrast you want to explore.</p></article><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">02 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Tune the transfer</h3><p>Explore the strength and look controls in Grade&#x27;s actual workspace.</p></article><p class="tcc-story-status tcc-story-sr-only" data-story-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Begin with a reference</h3><p>Use color statistics from a still to explore a new direction.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Compare as you adjust</h3><p>Check the before/after split and dial back the intensity.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Take the look elsewhere</h3><p>Export a .cube LUT or a graded PNG still.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A warmer portrait</option><option value="1">A cool performance look</option><option value="2">A subtle LUT</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A warmer portrait</h3><p>Explore a restrained color shift without losing the subject.</p><ol><li>Load a portrait and a warm reference still you have rights to use.</li><li>Start with Balanced transfer and lower intensity until skin looks believable.</li><li>Compare before/after and export a PNG still.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A cool performance look</h3><p>Test a reference palette against a video clip.</p><ol><li>Import the clip and a reference with the colors you want.</li><li>Compare transfer methods and review multiple moments in the clip.</li><li>Export a .cube LUT and test it on the same source footage.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">A subtle LUT</h3><p>Learn how much a reference should influence the result.</p><ol><li>Use source and reference images with similar exposure.</li><li>Compare low and high intensity while watching shadows and skin.</li><li>Export the LUT; treat it as source-specific, not a universal preset.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://scenepilot.thecreatingco.com/tools/grade/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Grade <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Download the LUT and keep the original media and reference. Session-only previews are not saved grading projects.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>.cube LUT</dt><dd>17, 33 or 65 size; test it in the receiving editor.</dd></div><div><dt>PNG still</dt><dd>A graded image you can inspect or edit further.</dd></div><div><dt>ScenePilot import</dt><dd>Check the receiving editor&#x27;s save and compatibility behavior.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=grade#feedback">Send Grade feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>This is color transfer, not relighting or skin-aware grading. It assumes Rec.709/sRGB, not log or HDR. Histogram mode can posterize flat references. Cross-editor round-trips are not broadly qualified.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Download the LUT and keep the original media and reference. Session-only previews are not saved grading projects.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
