 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Bring a batch</h3><p>Analyze multiple tracks rather than repeating a one-file workflow.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Read the musical context</h3><p>Compare key, Camelot notation and tempo estimates in one list.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Keep the results</h3><p>Export CSV for reference or a compatible downstream workflow.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">Prepare a small DJ crate</option><option value="1">Check a known track</option><option value="2">Find a rehearsal tempo</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">Prepare a small DJ crate</h3><p>Compare a handful of tracks before planning transitions.</p><ol><li>Import five or six tracks with contrasting tempos.</li><li>Review the key, Camelot and BPM estimates for each track.</li><li>Export CSV and audition promising transitions by ear.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">Check a known track</h3><p>Learn how an estimate compares with a reference you trust.</p><ol><li>Analyze a song whose key and tempo you already know.</li><li>Check whether the tempo lands at half or double time.</li><li>Treat differences as a reason to listen, not proof that the reference is wrong.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">Find a rehearsal tempo</h3><p>Use an estimate to begin practicing a part.</p><ol><li>Import a recording with a clear pulse.</li><li>Compare the estimated BPM with a metronome and the actual groove.</li><li>Keep a CSV note, then adjust the practice tempo yourself.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://sattarimusic.com/studio/keybpm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Key &amp; BPM <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Export the CSV before closing the tool. Check the import requirements of any software you want to use it with.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>CSV</dt><dd>Track names with estimated key, Camelot and BPM.</dd></div><div><dt>Batch results</dt><dd>A reference list, not automatic DJ-library synchronization.</dd></div><div><dt>Musical review</dt><dd>Confirm uncertain estimates by ear.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=key-bpm#feedback">Send Key &amp; BPM feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>One global key estimate does not describe key changes, modal or atonal music. BPM may land at half or double time. Rough results are fallback estimates. The analyzer is fixture-tested, not benchmarked on a labeled music corpus.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Export the CSV before closing the tool. Check the import requirements of any software you want to use it with.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
