ts/luma-workshops/compose-example.jpg", "key": "luma:compose"}, {"product": "form", "id": "history", "title": "See how it was made", "description": "Explore the prepared See how it was made project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "History / sketch / extrude / bevel", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Inspect how the object\u2019s features build its shape.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=history", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:history"}, {"product": "luma", "id": "effects", "title": "Same layers. A different feeling.", "description": "Continue your composition and explore all 27 blend modes, 17 layer effects and 15 editable smart filters.", "skills": "Blending / opacity / layer effects / smart filters / blend modes", "level": "Explore", "time": "6\u20139 min", "firstMove": "Keep your eight-layer composition and try a blend mode or layer effect.", "url": "/learn/luma/workshops/?workshop=effects", "poster": "/assets/luma-workshops/effects-example.jpg", "key": "luma:effects"}, {"product": "form", "id": "challenge", "title": "Three objects, one workflow", "description": "Explore the prepared Three objects, one workflow project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Clasp / ring / enclosure / CAD", "level": "Explore", "firstMove": "Try the measured workflow on another object.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=challenge", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:challenge"}, {"product": "form", "id": "materials", "title": "Find the right finish", "description": "Explore the prepared Find the right finish project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Materials / finish / roughness / lighting", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Change the finish while keeping the shape.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=materials", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:materials"}, {"product": "form", "id": "handoff", "title": "Keep the editable object", "description": "Explore the prepared Keep the editable object project in the real Form Studio workspace. Keep an editable .form or garment file with native Save.", "skills": "Save / project / export / PNG / STL", "level": "First steps", "firstMove": "Keep an editable project and test an export.", "url": "/learn/form/workshops/?lesson=handoff", "poster": "/assets/after-hours/outputs/orbit-steel-render.png", "key": "form:handoff"}]}</script><details class="secondary-reference"><summary>Explore the workflow &amp; tools<span>Open guide ↗</span></summary><div class="suite-origin"><section class="suite-section" id="suite-workflow" aria-labelledby="suite-workflow-heading"><div class="suite-section-heading"><p class="suite-eyebrow">01 / THE WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="suite-workflow-heading">Follow the image.<br><span>Find your language.</span></h2><p class="suite-section-intro">Start with a useful change. Keep the layers, masks and lettering editable as the image grows.</p></div><div class="suite-steps"><article><span class="suite-step-number">01</span><h3>Start with what you have.</h3><p>Bring in a photograph, artwork or texture. Make a selection and isolate the part you want to change.</p><small>Image import / Selections / Masks</small></article><article><span class="suite-step-number">02</span><h3>Build the composition.</h3><p>Arrange images, add editable type and paint with captured brushes. Let layers and blending connect the pieces.</p><small>Layers / Typography / Captured brushes</small></article><article><span class="suite-step-number">03</span><h3>Find the feeling.</h3><p>Explore color and effects, compare a new direction and keep the editable project alongside your export.</p><small>Adjustments / Effects / Editable projects</small></article></div></section><section class="suite-features" id="suite-capabilities" aria-labelledby="suite-capabilities-heading"><div class="suite-feature-title"><p class="suite-eyebrow">02 / BUILT TO KEEP YOU MAKING</p><h2 id="suite-capabilities-heading">Bold images.<br><span>Editable decisions.</span></h2><p>Make a print. Build a campaign. Give one photograph three different moods. Choose the tools that serve the image.</p><a class="suite-text-link" href="#learn-studio">Find your starting point <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="suite-feature-list"><article><span class="suite-feature-number">01</span><div><p class="suite-eyebrow">Layers &amp; masks</p><h3>Change just the right part.</h3><p>Reorder the composition, refine a smart selection and paint a mask to control where a layer or adjustment appears.</p></div></article><article><span class="suite-feature-number">02</span><div><p class="suite-eyebrow">Brushes &amp; blending</p><h3>Make it belong.</h3><p>Capture an image as a brush. Blend a graphic into fabric, reveal texture and balance the opacity of each layer.</p></div></article><article><span class="suite-feature-number">03</span><div><p class="suite-eyebrow">Type &amp; composition</p><h3>Give the image a voice.</h3><p>Keep headlines editable, work with shapes and paths, and develop coordinated layouts from the same artwork.</p></div></article></div></section><section class="suite-fabric suite-section" id="suite-deeper" aria-labelledby="suite-deeper-heading"><div><p class="suite-eyebrow">03 / BEYOND ONE IMAGE</p><h2 id="suite-deeper-heading">One idea.<br><span>Many expressions.</span></h2><p class="suite-section-intro">Carry your visual language into a print, a shirt, an album cover or a poster. The prepared projects show how the pieces fit together.</p><a class="suite-text-link" href="#learn-studio">Try it in Luma Studio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="suite-fabric-notes"><span class="suite-label">REAL LUMA PROJECTS · EDITABLE LAYERS</span><dl><div><dt>Select</dt><dd>Recolor a shirt through a mask while retaining the photograph underneath.</dd></div><div><dt>Compose</dt><dd>Reorder eight separate layers and find a different balance.</dd></div><div><dt>Explore</dt><dd>Compare effects and blend modes on the same layered composition.</dd></div></dl><p class="suite-fineprint">The workshops combine source images with additional editable layers, masks, type and treatments. Keep the original photograph and save your editable .luma project.</p></div></section></div></details><!-- PRODUCT-REFRESH:START --><!-- PRODUCT-REFRESH:END --><!-- LUMA-WORKSHOPS:START --><!-- PRODUCT-LESSONS:START --><!-- PRODUCT-LESSONS:END --><!-- LUMA-WORKSHOPS:END --><div class="section" style="padding-block:0"></div><!-- PRODUCT-FEATURES:START --><section class="pf" id="product-features" aria-labelledby="pf-title" data-product-features="luma" style="--pf-accent:#ff83ba"><div class="pf-intro"><div><p class="pf-eyebrow">INSIDE LUMA STUDIO</p><h2 id="pf-title">What Luma Studio can do.</h2><p class="pf-lede">Build layered images, refine every detail, and keep creative decisions editable.</p></div><p class="pf-total"><strong>21</strong><span>features to explore</span></p></div><aside class="pf-scope" aria-label="Edition and availability"><p><strong>Full product inventory. Web, native and experimental capabilities vary by edition.</strong> Hosted generative edits require authentication and network access. Desktop RAW support and native processing go beyond the browser. PSD/PSB conversion is explicitly scoped rather than universally lossless.</p></aside><div class="pr-search"><label for="pr-feature-search">Find a capability</label><input id="pr-feature-search" type="search" data-pr-search placeholder="Search tools, workflows or editions" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="pr-feature-status"><p id="pr-feature-status" data-pr-search-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><nav class="pf-jump" aria-label="Feature categories"><a href="#pf-luma-1">Layers &amp; color</a><a href="#pf-luma-2">Paint, select &amp; compose</a><a href="#pf-luma-3">RAW &amp; Photoshop workflows</a><a href="#pf-luma-4">Production &amp; creative continuity</a></nav><details class="pf-group" id="pf-luma-1"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Layers &amp; color</h3><span class="pf-group-count">6 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Complete layer system</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Raster, text, shape, path, group, adjustment, and smart-object layers.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=compose#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Advanced blending</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>27 Photoshop layer blend modes, opacity and fill controls, multiple blend passes, and Blend If.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=effects#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Masks and effects</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Layer masks, clipping masks, layer effects, and editable smart filters.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=campaign#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Nondestructive adjustments</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Levels, Curves, HSL, exposure, tone, and color adjustments.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=grade#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Precision color</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>8-, 16-, and 32-bit precision masters; sRGB, Display P3, and linear sRGB working spaces.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=grade#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Color management</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Supported ICC profiles, soft proofing, and gamut warnings.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-luma-2"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Paint, select &amp; compose</h3><span class="pf-group-count">7 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Painting</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Pressure- and tilt-aware brushes, symmetry, painting, erasing, and mixer tools.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=print#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases="captured brush capture motif stamp pattern"><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Custom brushes</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Capture full-color image tips from the canvas or an uploaded image; use tint or stencil modes and save brush libraries inside projects.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=print#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Retouching</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Clone, healing, removal, dodge/burn, blur/sharpen, smudge, and sponge tools.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=rescue#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases="smart select smart selection shirt recolor mask"><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Selections</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Marquee, lasso, polygonal, magnetic, color, quick, text-mask, and local semantic selections.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=recolor#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Selection refinement</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Feathering, smoothing, contrast, and edge shifting.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=recolor#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Typography</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Editable text, paragraph and vertical type, and text on curved paths.</p><p class="feature-availability">Try the browser workshop online. Initial editor and example assets require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=weave#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Vector and composition tools</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Pen and direct selection, shapes, perspective adjustments, cropping, straightening, and transforms.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=stickers#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-luma-3"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>RAW &amp; Photoshop workflows</h3><span class="pf-group-count">3 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>RAW development</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Supported DNG sensor development with retained source data, white balance, exposure, and highlight controls.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Desktop camera support</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Additional camera formats through available macOS codecs, with clearly identified preview fallbacks.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Photoshop interchange</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>PSD/PSB preflight, preservation of supported text/vector/adjustment metadata and smart-object payloads, plus conversion warnings.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details><details class="pf-group" id="pf-luma-4"><summary><span class="pf-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Production &amp; creative continuity</h3><span class="pf-group-count">5 features</span></summary><ul class="pf-feature-list"><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Versioning and workspace</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Branching history, recovery, multiple documents, contextual properties, custom workspaces, and shortcuts.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Production tools</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Actions, batch ZIP export, named layer comps, channel inspection, and artboard-region export.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>AI-assisted editing</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Local segmentation/matting and authenticated hosted generative edits, including masked regions and variations.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Saving and export</h4><span class="pf-edition">Browser workshop / edition varies</span></div><p>Editable `.luma` projects and PNG, JPEG, and WebP outputs.</p><p class="feature-availability">Available in the browser workshop. Initial editor and media loading require a network connection.</p><a class="pf-example-link" href="/products/luma/?lesson=identity#learn-studio">Try this feature ↗</a></li><li class="pf-feature" data-feature-aliases=""><div class="pf-feature-heading"><h4>Desktop extensions</h4><span class="pf-edition">Edition varies</span></div><p>Declarative action packages, native file dialogs, and native high-precision compositing for eligible documents.</p><p class="feature-availability">See release status for this edition. Offline operation is not confirmed for this capability.</p></li></ul></details></section><!-- PRODUCT-FEATURES:END --><!-- AFTER-HOURS:luma:START --><details class="secondary-reference"><summary>Project walkthrough: After Hours<span>Open reference ↗</span></summary><section class="ah" id="after-hours-luma" data-after-hours="luma" style="--ah-accent:#6148bd"><p class="ah-eyebrow">AFTER HOURS / Luma Studio / Web editor</p><h2>An image becomes an invitation.</h2><p class="ah-deck">Build a real exhibition poster: one original still life, two editable text elements, and a controlled shift in tone.</p><div class="ah-chapters" role="tablist" aria-label="After Hours Exhibition Poster chapters"><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-luma-tab-0" aria-controls="after-hours-luma-panel-0" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0"><span>01</span>Begin with an image</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-luma-tab-1" aria-controls="after-hours-luma-panel-1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>02</span>Give it a voice</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-luma-tab-2" aria-controls="after-hours-luma-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>03</span>Develop the atmosphere</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="after-hours-luma-tab-3" aria-controls="after-hours-luma-panel-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>04</span>Keep every decision</button></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-luma-panel-0" aria-labelledby="after-hours-luma-tab-0" ><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/luma-01-source.png" alt="Luma Studio: Begin with an image. An original AI-generated still life becomes a 1024 × 1536 portrait document. The source artwork remains its own raster layer." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Begin with an image</h3><p>An original AI-generated still life becomes a 1024 × 1536 portrait document. The source artwork remains its own raster layer.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-luma-panel-1" aria-labelledby="after-hours-luma-tab-1" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/luma-02-type.png" alt="Luma Studio: Give it a voice. AFTER HOURS and OBJECTS / SOUND / IDEAS are separate editable text elements, placed in the open space around the still life." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Give it a voice</h3><p>AFTER HOURS and OBJECTS / SOUND / IDEAS are separate editable text elements, placed in the open space around the still life.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-luma-panel-2" aria-labelledby="after-hours-luma-tab-2" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/luma-03-tone.png" alt="Luma Studio: Develop the atmosphere. A tone layer sets exposure to 0.20, contrast to 12, shadows to 8 and temperature to −8. The before and after views use the same composition." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Develop the atmosphere</h3><p>A tone layer sets exposure to 0.20, contrast to 12, shadows to 8 and temperature to −8. The before and after views use the same composition.</p></div></div><div role="tabpanel" id="after-hours-luma-panel-3" aria-labelledby="after-hours-luma-tab-3" hidden><div class="ah-stage"><img src="/assets/after-hours/luma-04-finished.png" alt="Luma Studio: Keep every decision. The four-layer document was saved in Luma’s native format. Its exported PNG was opened and visually checked at the original 1024 × 1536 size." width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-caption"><h3>Keep every decision</h3><p>The four-layer document was saved in Luma’s native format. Its exported PNG was opened and visually checked at the original 1024 × 1536 size.</p></div></div><p class="ah-count" data-ah-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="ah-actions"><a class="ah-primary" href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open Luma Studio ↗</a><button type="button" data-ah-expand>Inspect the screenshot</button><button type="button" data-ah-toggle-compare aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="after-hours-luma-compare">Compare the tone</button></div><div class="ah-output" id="after-hours-luma-compare" data-ah-comparison hidden><h3>Compare the tone</h3><div class="ah-compare"><img src="/assets/after-hours/luma-before-tone.png" alt="Original tone" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"><img class="ah-after" src="/assets/after-hours/luma-03-tone.png" alt="Developed tone" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ah-compare-labels"><span>Original tone</span><span>Developed tone</span></div><label for="after-hours-luma-range">Comparison divider <output for="after-hours-luma-range">50%</output></label><input class="ah-comparison-control" id="after-hours-luma-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Comparison divider"></div><div class="ah-output ah-result"><div><h3>The finished invitation</h3><p>Actual PNG output from Luma. The source artwork was AI-generated; typography and tone were applied in the editor.</p></div><img src="/assets/after-hours/outputs/after-hours-poster.png" alt="The finished invitation" loading="lazy" width="1024" height="1536"></div><div class="ah-actions"><a href="/assets/after-hours/outputs/after-hours-poster.png" download>Download the poster</a><a href="/assets/after-hours/outputs/after-hours-poster.luma" download>Download the editable project</a></div><p class="ah-note">Actual browser session. Native Luma v4 archive integrity and all four layer records were verified. No PSD round-trip or print-production fidelity is implied.</p><dialog aria-labelledby="after-hours-luma-dialog-title"><button type="button" autofocus>Close screenshot</button><p id="after-hours-luma-dialog-title" data-ah-dialog-title></p><img alt=""></dialog></section></details><!-- AFTER-HOURS:luma:END --><section class="scope-section section" id="browser"><div><p class="overline">YOUR BROWSER EDITION</p><h2>Your web edition.</h2><p>Paint, compose with layers, adjust color, and export an image using the shared Luma editing engine.</p><details open><summary>Current limitations</summary><p>Native RAW codecs and desktop print features are not all available in the browser. Optional hosted generative edits require sign-in and send selected image content to a service. PSD conversions have limits.</p></details></div><div class="try-card"><h3>One good first test</h3><ol><li><span>01</span>Start a document or import your own image.</li><li><span>02</span>Paint or add an editable layer.</li><li><span>03</span>Export an image and keep a .luma project.</li></ol><a class="button accent primary-app" href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open the browser app</a><a href="/testing/?product=luma#feedback">Send feedback</a></div></section><section class="section prose" id="new-tools"><p class="overline">NEW IN LUMA STUDIO</p><h2>Mockup and Glyph, in the &ldquo;&hellip;&rdquo; menu.</h2><p>Both are public web alpha, inside the same Luma Studio you already use.</p><h3 id="mockup">Mockup</h3><p>Put your art onto a tee, hoodie, tote, poster, vinyl sleeve, or phone case, then batch-export every scene as PNG or JPEG. Scenes are procedural illustrations, not photographed products. Open Luma Studio, then use the &ldquo;&hellip;&rdquo; menu &rarr; Mockups. <a href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open Luma Studio <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a> &middot; <a href="/products/mockup/">More about Mockup</a></p><h3 id="glyph">Glyph</h3><p>Draw your own letterforms with brush or pen tools and export OTF/TTF. Installed fonts now embed in <code>.luma</code> projects so they reopen anywhere, and the font shows up directly in Luma&rsquo;s type tool. Open Luma Studio, then use the &ldquo;&hellip;&rdquo; menu &rarr; Glyph font maker. <a href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio">Open Luma Studio <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a> &middot; <a href="/products/glyph/">More about Glyph</a></p></section><!-- PRODUCT-NEXT:START --><section class="pr-next" aria-labelledby="pr-next-title"><p class="pr-kicker">THE FOUR-PRODUCT CREATIVE SUITE</p><h2 id="pr-next-title">Keep the idea moving.</h2><div class="pr-cards"><a class="pr-card" href="/products/form/" style="--pr-tone:#d8ff3e"><h3>Form Studio</h3><p>Give your next idea a dimension.</p><span class="pr-card-label">Explore the product<b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><a class="pr-card" href="/products/stemdeck/" style="--pr-tone:#ffb05e"><h3>StemDeck</h3><p>Find the mix. Make the moment.</p><span class="pr-card-label">Explore the product<b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><a class="pr-card" href="/products/scenepilot/" style="--pr-tone:#b8a3ff"><h3>ScenePilot</h3><p>Your footage. Your rhythm. Your film.</p><span class="pr-card-label">Explore the product<b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a></div></section><!-- PRODUCT-NEXT:END --></main><footer class="mm-footer cc-footer"><div><a class="wordmark" href="/start/">thecreateco.</a><p>For whatever you are into next.</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer"><section aria-labelledby="footer-0"><h2 id=