y-visual><div class="tcc-story-frames"><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-mockup-1" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/creative-tools/mockups.webp" alt="Mockup starting workspace for artwork placement." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Mockup starting workspace for artwork placement.</figcaption></figure><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-mockup-2" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/tool-products/mockups.webp" alt="Stylized procedural mockup exported as a PNG, not a photograph." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Stylized procedural mockup exported as a PNG, not a photograph.</figcaption></figure></div><nav class="tcc-story-controls" data-story-controls role="tablist" aria-label="Mockup visual tour" hidden></nav></div><div class="tcc-story-copy"><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Bring in artwork</h3><p>Start with a design you want to see on a product surface.</p></article><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">02 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Explore the scene</h3><p>Review an exported example; the in-app preview may vary by browser.</p></article><p class="tcc-story-status tcc-story-sr-only" data-story-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Six places for one idea</h3><p>Compare the same artwork across six stylized product scenes.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Placement that stays yours</h3><p>Adjust scale, rotation, position, product color and ink density.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Keep the presentation editable</h3><p>Open a result as a Luma document or export images and a ZIP.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A small merch collection</option><option value="1">An album artwork set</option><option value="2">A colorway comparison</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A small merch collection</h3><p>Compare one graphic on a tee, hoodie and tote.</p><ol><li>Open your artwork in Luma, then choose Mockups from the studio menu.</li><li>Adjust placement on the tee and compare how it reads on other products.</li><li>Export the scenes as a ZIP and inspect them side by side.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">An album artwork set</h3><p>Present a cover as a sleeve and a wall poster.</p><ol><li>Use a finished artwork document or upload an image inside Mockups.</li><li>Compare the vinyl sleeve and poster scenes; adjust scale separately.</li><li>Open a result as a document to add final presentation details.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">A colorway comparison</h3><p>Find a product color that supports the artwork.</p><ol><li>Choose one scene and a graphic with a clear silhouette.</li><li>Try different product colors and check ink density and contrast.</li><li>Download your preferred scene as PNG or JPEG.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://luma.thecreatingco.com/studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Mockup <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a><p class="tp-entry">In Luma Studio, open the studio menu and choose Mockups.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Download the image set and save your original Luma document. Mockup scenes are not editable garment patterns.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>PNG / JPEG</dt><dd>Individual scenes, up to the tool&#x27;s 2000px option.</dd></div><div><dt>ZIP</dt><dd>Download the full six-scene set.</dd></div><div><dt>Luma document</dt><dd>Open a rendered scene for further editing.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=mockup#feedback">Send Mockup feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>These are stylized procedural scenes, not photographs or physically simulated garments. Folds, fabric and glare are approximations. Use them to present a direction, not certify print placement or manufacturing results.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Download the image set and save your original Luma document. Mockup scenes are not editable garment patterns.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
