 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>A beat under your fingers</h3><p>Program six synthesized drum voices and one bass voice.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Find the feel</h3><p>Adjust tempo, swing, key and scale, then balance the mixer.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Keep the idea moving</h3><p>Export a loop or stems, or use the StemDeck handoff.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A late-night groove</option><option value="1">A rhythm comparison</option><option value="2">Parts for StemDeck</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A late-night groove</h3><p>Start with a sparse kick, hat and bass pattern.</p><ol><li>Tap a few kick hits, then add hats and a snare or clap.</li><li>Add bass notes, choose a scale and experiment with swing.</li><li>Balance the voices and export the loop.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A rhythm comparison</h3><p>Learn how small timing choices change a beat.</p><ol><li>Build a simple straight pattern at a comfortable tempo.</li><li>Compare different swing amounts without changing the notes.</li><li>Export the version whose feel you prefer.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">Parts for StemDeck</h3><p>Carry a sketch into a larger audio session.</p><ol><li>Create a drum and bass pattern and check each voice in the mixer.</li><li>Download stems as a backup.</li><li>Send to StemDeck and confirm the parts arrive before leaving Pocket.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://sattarimusic.com/studio/pocket" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Pocket <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Export important ideas. Clearing site data can remove locally saved patterns; browser storage is not an account backup.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>WAV loop</dt><dd>A rendered sketch of the pattern.</dd></div><div><dt>Individual stems</dt><dd>Separate parts for further mixing.</dd></div><div><dt>StemDeck handoff</dt><dd>Continue with the Sattari audio workspace.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=pocket#feedback">Send Pocket feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>One 16-step bar per pattern; no song mode or pattern chaining. Sounds are synthesized, not sampled kits. Patterns live in local browser storage. Background tabs can drift, and physical-phone audio/download behavior still needs qualification.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Export important ideas. Clearing site data can remove locally saved patterns; browser storage is not an account backup.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
