tive-tools/vox.webp" alt="Vox starting workspace for a vocal recording." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Vox starting workspace for a vocal recording.</figcaption></figure><figure class="tcc-story-frame" id="product-story-vox-2" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" data-story-frame><img src="/assets/tool-products/vox.webp" alt="Vox actual workspace capture showing vocal-correction controls." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Vox actual workspace capture showing vocal-correction controls.</figcaption></figure></div><nav class="tcc-story-controls" data-story-controls role="tablist" aria-label="Vox visual tour" hidden></nav></div><div class="tcc-story-copy"><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Start with a vocal</h3><p>Record or import a dry take to work from.</p></article><article class="tcc-story-step" data-story-step><p class="tcc-story-count">02 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 02</p><h3>Shape the result</h3><p>Explore pitch and harmony controls, then keep a downloaded WAV.</p></article><p class="tcc-story-status tcc-story-sr-only" data-story-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OUTPUT</p><h2 id="features-title">Make it your own.</h2><div class="tp-features"><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">01</span><h3>Start with one voice</h3><p>Record in the browser or import a clean, monophonic take.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">02</span><h3>Choose how far to push it</h3><p>Set the scale and compare light and stronger correction.</p></div><div class="tp-feature"><span class="tp-number">03</span><h3>Try a harmony</h3><p>Explore a generated third or fifth that follows the lead.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-making" id="make" aria-labelledby="make-title"><span id="how-it-works"></span><div class="tp-inner"><p class="tp-eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2 id="make-title">One tool. Three starting points.</h2><div class="tp-lesson" data-tp-player><div class="tp-lesson-toolbar" data-tp-controls hidden><label for="project-picker">Project</label><select id="project-picker" data-tp-picker><option value="0">A gentle vocal correction</option><option value="1">A harmony sketch</option><option value="2">A deliberately synthetic voice</option></select><div class="tp-cycle"><button type="button" data-tp-previous aria-label="Previous project" title="Previous project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button><span data-tp-count role="status" aria-live="polite">1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-tp-next aria-label="Next project" title="Next project"><svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></button></div></div><div class="tp-lesson-content"><article data-tp-lesson aria-labelledby="lesson-0"><h3 id="lesson-0">A gentle vocal correction</h3><p>Hear what changes when the correction stays restrained.</p><ol><li>Record a short a cappella phrase without a backing track.</li><li>Check the key and compare light correction with the original.</li><li>Export the take and listen for artifacts before using it in a mix.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-1"><h3 id="lesson-1">A harmony sketch</h3><p>Test a supporting interval before recording another singer.</p><ol><li>Import a clean lead vocal and choose its intended scale.</li><li>Compare a third and a fifth against the original melody.</li><li>Use the export as a sketch, not an independent vocal performance.</li></ol></article><article data-tp-lesson hidden aria-labelledby="lesson-2"><h3 id="lesson-2">A deliberately synthetic voice</h3><p>Explore stronger correction as a creative texture.</p><ol><li>Use a short phrase with clearly pitched notes.</li><li>Raise correction strength and audition the result.</li><li>Export WAV and keep the unprocessed take so you can revisit the choice.</li></ol></article></div><div class="tp-lesson-footer"><a class="tp-primary" href="https://sattarimusic.com/studio/vox" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Make it in Vox <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band" id="exports" aria-labelledby="exports-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-export-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">YOUR WORK, TO KEEP</p><h2 id="exports-title">Take the result with you.</h2><p>Keep the original recording and download your processed WAV. Do not rely on the open tab as your only copy.</p></div><dl class="tp-exports"><div><dt>WAV</dt><dd>Download the processed vocal result.</dd></div><div><dt>Recording / import</dt><dd>Keep an original dry take separately.</dd></div><div><dt>Offline processing</dt><dd>Not live correction while singing.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
 <section class="tp-band tp-notes" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div class="tp-inner tp-note-layout"><div><p class="tp-eyebrow">BUILDING IN PUBLIC</p><h2 id="limits-title">An alpha. An invitation.</h2><p>Try it, make something, and tell us what needs to work better.</p><a class="tp-feedback" href="/testing/?product=vox#feedback">Send Vox feedback <svg class="lucide" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M10 14 21 3"/><path d="M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg></a></div><div class="tp-questions"><details open><summary>What should I know before starting?</summary><p>Backing tracks, reverb and polyphonic audio can confuse pitch tracking. Large corrections and harmonies may sound phasey or robotic. The harmony follows the lead rather than creating an independent performance.</p></details><details><summary>How do I keep my work?</summary><p>Keep the original recording and download your processed WAV. Do not rely on the open tab as your only copy.</p></details><details><summary>Can I download a native app?</summary><p>This page opens the public web alpha. There are no public native downloads yet. <a href="/downloads/">Check current availability.</a></p></details></div></div></section>
